mpv 0.42.0 fails to compile for macOS with Cocoa and Swift on and Vulkan
off, which is how packaging/macos-libmpv-build.sh builds it: View's
isOpaque refers to MetalLayer, a class defined in
video/out/mac/metal_layer.swift, which meson.build compiles only when
Vulkan is on. The reference came in after 0.41.0, and mpv's issue 18357,
which reports the error, was closed without a fix. This puts it behind
HAVE_VULKAN, which mpv's meson defines for the Swift compiler whenever
Vulkan is on, so a build without Vulkan takes the view as opaque, as it
would for any layer that isn't a MetalLayer. Patina renders through the
render API into its own OpenGL context and never shows mpv's window, so
this code doesn't run for it at all.

Applied with `patch -p1` in the unpacked source. Drop it once an mpv
release compiles without it.

--- a/video/out/mac/view.swift
+++ b/video/out/mac/view.swift
@@ -29,9 +29,11 @@
     override var acceptsFirstResponder: Bool { return true }
 
     override var isOpaque: Bool {
+#if HAVE_VULKAN
         if let metalLayer = layer as? MetalLayer {
             return !metalLayer.isOpaque
         }
+#endif
 
         return true
     }
